# Role
Act as a senior frontend engineer and technical architect.

# Project
Build a professional veterinary hospital website for Riverside Veterinary Hospital in Chattanooga, Tennessee.

# Technology
- Nuxt 4
- Vue 3 Composition API
- TypeScript
- Tailwind CSS
- Nuxt conventions and reusable components

# Architecture
- Keep components modular and reusable.
- Separate business content and service data from presentation.
- Avoid duplicated code.
- Use clear naming conventions.
- Keep pages lightweight.
- Avoid unnecessary dependencies.
- Do not introduce a backend unless required.

# Design
- Premium, trustworthy veterinary brand.
- Forest green, medical blue, deep navy, warm ivory, and warm sand. Soft sage as a quiet support. Colors are assigned to roles, not scattered.
- Responsive, mobile-first design.
- Strong typography and visual hierarchy.
- Professional veterinary photography.
- Clear appointment and telephone CTAs.

# Quality
- Semantic HTML.
- Accessible forms and navigation.
- SEO metadata on every page.
- Optimized images and performance.
- No broken links or placeholder buttons.
- Validate forms and provide meaningful feedback.
- Never invent real business contact information.
- Clearly distinguish demo functionality from live integrations.

# Development workflow
- Inspect existing files before changing configuration.
- Implement incrementally.
- Run the project and verify changes.
- Fix errors before moving to the next major feature.
- Avoid unnecessary abstractions and overengineering.
- Prioritize a complete working MVP within the time limit.
